WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.770
Deadpool 2 was bigger, louder, and packed
with even more insanity than the original

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.770
Deadpool.

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:09.970
Still, for as bombastic as the movie was,
there were a surprising number of subtle references

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.170
and obscure characters adapted for the big
screen.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:17.610
From a lesson on box office history to quick
nods to comic book continuity, here are small

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.190
details you missed in Deadpool 2.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.400
"And I hope you're watching!"

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.940
R-rated domination
In Deadpool 2, the Merc with a Mouth acknowledges

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.190
the success of Deadpool by telling the audience
about the box office history of some of the

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:34.809
highest-grossing R-rated movies.

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:39.579
That lesson wouldn't be complete without mentioning
the highest-grossing R-rated movie in U.S.

00:00:39.579 --> 00:00:42.129
box office history: The Passion of the Christ.

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:46.809
The film earned an astonishing domestic gross
of over $370 million.

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:50.530
While Mel Gibson's biblical epic might never
get toppled from its throne in terms of how

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:54.420
much it made in America, it's a different
story internationally.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:01:00.249
Deadpool managed to earn a staggering $783
million worldwide, making the violent superhero

00:01:00.249 --> 00:01:03.719
romp the highest-grossing R-rated international
film of all time.

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:07.530
Not bad for a character that once got beat
up by Squirrel Girl.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:11.150
Pryor's Treats
X-Men continuity is generally a confusing

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:16.280
mess spread through dozens of comic series,
as well as decades of retcons and unusual,

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.479
complicated familial revelations.

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:22.770
Even within that knot of continuity, there's
arguably no character with a more complicated

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.649
family history than Cable.

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:28.969
As the son of Scott Summers and a clone of
Jean Grey named Madelyne Pryor, Nathaniel

00:01:28.969 --> 00:01:33.310
Summers has been to the future, was infected
with a techno-organic virus by a powerful

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:37.720
supervillain, and even fled through time protecting
a little girl that looks suspiciously like

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:38.720
his own mother.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.400
In short, he's pretty complicated.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.150
While Deadpool 2 stays away from too many
blatant Easter Eggs involving Josh Brolin's

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.979
Cable, there are quick references to his comic
book roots.

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:52.170
Immediately after most of the newly-formed
X-Force parachutes into a suburban neighborhood

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:57.039
and meet their untimely demises, an ice cream
truck can be seen with a logo reading "Pryor's

00:01:57.039 --> 00:02:01.290
Treats," referring to Cable's biological mother,
Madelyne Pryor.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:04.970
House of M
Deadpool's no stranger to twisted timelines

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:08.340
himself, as his dialogue in both Deadpool
and Deadpool 2 would suggest.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.220
"Let us go talk to the professor."

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:12.820
"McAvoy or Stewart?

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.520
These timelines are so confusing."

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:20.140
From metatextual knowledge of Professor Xavier's
different actors to his blasé relationship

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.630
with time-travel, the Merc with a Mouth seems
to take it all in stride.

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:27.110
Still, maybe he should have been a little
more worried about the banners that hung inside

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.710
the Essex House that read "M-Day is Coming."

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:34.160
Long-time comic readers might remember that
M-Day is the in-universe term for when Scarlet

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:38.650
Witch erases the mutant genome in House of
M. M-Day goes down in Marvel history as a

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:43.130
dark time for mutants, since the resulting
wipe of the mutant race sticks around for

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:44.130
years.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.650
The mutant population in the Marvel universe
actually drops from tens of thousands all

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.090
the way to just a couple hundred.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:54.510
For years, the mutant population slowly dwindles,
right until a very important mutant baby is

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:55.510
born.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:56.510
That mutant?

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:57.660
Hope Summers, Cable's daughter.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:01.900
No wonder Cable's so grumpy in the movie if
he's from such a grim future.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:05.750
Irene Merryweather
During Russell Collins' first fiery appearance

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:10.170
in Deadpool 2, even the on-scene reporter
is a supporting character who appeared in

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.400
the comic series Cable &amp; Deadpool.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.140
Like her movie counterpart, Irene Merryweather
is a reporter, but the comics version of the

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:20.690
character goes on a much wilder series of
adventures than her quick movie appearance

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:21.780
would suggest.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:26.230
She's been the chronicler of Cable's adventures,
a writer for the Daily Bugle, an object of

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:30.180
Deadpool's romantic affections, and the Chief
of Staff of an entire island-state.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.710
That's a heck of a resume.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:36.180
X-Men fan
While movie Deadpool can pretend to be too

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:40.510
cool for Xavier's school, comic book Deadpool
is a pretty big X-Men fan.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:44.150
Since Deadpool breaks the fourth wall more
often than the Wrecking Crew breaks actual

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:48.930
walls, this manifests in him referencing specific
issue numbers when he gets excited in Deadpool

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:49.930
2.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:53.460
When Juggernaut appears, the Merc with a Mouth
tells him how big a fan he is and names three

00:03:53.460 --> 00:04:01.180
Juggernaut-centric comic book issues: Uncanny
X-Men #183, X-Men Unlimited #12, and Thor

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.180
#411.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:06.250
Beyond just featuring the Juggernaut, all
three issues have a thematic connection, as

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:09.170
well; Juggernaut taking down increasingly
powerful enemies.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:15.000
In Uncanny X-Men #183, Juggernaut brings an
entire building down on Colossus in a bar

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.000
fight.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.530
In Thor #411, Juggernaut fights and completely
defeats Thor, the God of Thunder.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:25.460
Finally, in X-Men Unlimited #12, Juggernaut
fights the cosmic entity that controls his

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.710
power, Cytorrak, and defeats him too.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:31.790
If Deadpool's been reading these comics, it's
no wonder he's such a fan of Cain Marko.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:35.690
And when Deadpool says, quote, "It has always
been a dream of mine to see myself reflected

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:38.650
in your helmet as you charge at me with murderous
intent"?

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:42.820
Well that actually happened on the cover of
his own book, on Deadpool #2.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.060
Dreams really do come true.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:47.770
Beyond the comic book reference, there's a
very good reason for Deadpool to get excited

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:49.430
about fighting the Juggernaut.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:53.310
Much like having a tragic origin or joining
the Avengers, fighting the unstoppable force

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.680
of the Juggernaut is basically a rite of passage
in the Marvel universe.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.930
Colossus did it, Thor did it, even Spider-Man
has done it.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:01.450
Welcome to the big leagues, Wade Wilson.

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.450
Thanks for watching!

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:05.400
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.810
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

